# Set Home Alt switches the altitudes shown between above home and above sea level.
#
# BUT_Homealt_Click sets cs.altoffsethome to minus cs.HomeAlt when it is zero and back to zero
# when it is not; cs.alt, which the HUD and the quick view show, is `_alt - altoffsethome`. It
# sends nothing. `GCSViews/FlightData.cs:1236-1247, ExtLibs/ArduPilot/CurrentState.cs:325-328`
#
# cs.HomeAlt is HomeLocation.Alt, which only HOME_POSITION sets, and is 0 until then
# (CurrentState.cs:40, 1568-1582; MAVLinkInterface.cs:5701-5707). SITL sends HOME_POSITION of
# its own accord only when home is set - its first fix, or arming - so a run that joins a SITL
# whose home is already set hears none: Set Home Alt would then set minus zero, which reads as
# not set, and nothing would change (proven in fly.rs's
# set_home_alt_takes_the_home_the_vehicle_reported). So the test first asks for home as Mission
# Planner does without moving it: Set Home Here answered Cancel still calls getHomePositionAsync
# (FlightData.cs:4852-4885), which needs a terrain tile at the point, so the data directory here
# is a scratch one holding a flat tile at 584 m for SITL's field, as fly-sethome.gui does.
# SITL's field is 584 m above sea level, so HomeAlt, and every altitude shown on the ground with
# Set Home Alt on, is above 500; off, the altitude shown is the height above home, near 0.
#
# Needs SITL (a copter): tools/gui-test.sh tests/gui/fly-homealt.gui -- tcp:127.0.0.1:5760

env XDG_DATA_HOME $WORK
setup mkdir -p "$WORK/MissionPlannerRust/srtm" && python3 -c 'import sys; open(sys.argv[1], "wb").write(bytes([2, 72]) * (1201 * 1201))' "$WORK/MissionPlannerRust/srtm/S36E149.hgt"
screen fly
window 1600x1200
settle 8

# The first quick view is cs.alt, as it starts; the second is made cs.HomeAlt.
expect fly.quick.1 alt
doubleclick fly-quick-2
expect fly.quick.chooser 2
click fly-quick-choice-HomeAlt
expect fly.quick.2 HomeAlt

# The Actions grid is on the Actions page, tabActions; the strip opens on Quick, as
# tabControlactions.SelectedIndex = 0 has it. `GCSViews/FlightData.Designer.cs:595-611`
click fly-tab-actions
expect fly.tab tabActions

# Home asked for: the map pressed, Set Home Here, Cancel - home is not moved.
click map@0.5x0.5
click fly-sethome
expect fly.prompt This will reset the onboard home position (effects RTL etc). Are you Sure?
click fly-prompt-cancel
expect fly.prompt none
expect fly.sent COMMAND_LONG MAV_CMD_GET_HOME_POSITION 0,0,0,0,0,0,0
settle 2
expect fly.quick.2.value > 500
expect fly.quick.1.value < 50

# On: minus HomeAlt, so the altitude shown is above sea level.
expect fly.home_alt off
click fly-homealt
expect fly.home_alt on
expect status ~ above sea level
expect fly.quick.1.value > 500
# Off again: above home.
click fly-homealt
expect fly.home_alt off
expect status ~ above home
expect fly.quick.1.value < 50
